It is Thursday afternoon.
I am off from work.
I walk over to the bicycle mechanic.
The time is a quarter to four.
The mechanic is standing in the shop.
"Hi," I say.
He rolls the bicycle out to me.
"Your bike is ready," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
The bike looks really nice.
The tires are hard now.
I wheel the bike out onto the street.
The sun is shining today.
I get on the bike.
I often cycle in Copenhagen.
It is very easy.
Now I happily cycle towards the hairdresser.
My appointment is at half past four.
I am looking forward to it.
